{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall know that YHWH your Elohim, He is the Elohim, the faithful El.</b> You shall know from the Exodus from Egypt that YHWH your Elohim is the Elohim who created heaven and earth, and furthermore you shall know from this that He is the faithful El, that He is faithful to fulfill His covenant, because the power is in His hand. And it says <b>to the thousandth generation</b>, and elsewhere it says (Exodus 20:6) ״ועושה חסד לאלפים לאהבי״ — 'showing kindness to thousands of those who love Me.' Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: here it refers to those who act out of love; there it refers to those who act out of fear — this one is read in connection with what adjoins it, and that one is read in connection with what adjoins it. And from this you shall further know that He repays His enemies, to each one of His enemies."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:20.018276928Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}